Z||000004||lowCG||06-05-99||01:25 PM||||How about a Volkswagen Solex carb. on the F.I. manifold? Would seem to be a suitable level of technology considering you've clearly not decided to step up to the digital level.All you'd need to do is put a fuel return line with,say,a 1/8" restrictor inside of it and some form of a linkeage.Might even run better,provided you haven't screwed up anything that the ignition would need to function.Even then,an old sunbird distributor(HEI)might fit the bill.Good luck,and hide the hammer!
Z||000005||grizco||06-08-99||05:04 PM||||If he's pulled the ECM there's no way for the distributor to advance as needed. Also to put a carberator on hell need to add a pressure regulator of some sort to the fuel system since the carberator will flood out at idle with anything more than around 7 psi.
Z||000006||theogre||06-08-99||07:40 PM||||Nope, no vac advance on that dist..... It'll be a real pile of crap trying to accelerate w/o it too. I don't think those even have centrifical advance on them. Would need a dist off a carb version of the motor... good luck finding that.<p>would be better to put all the damn thing back the way it was built and learn how to do it right this time.............
